# Icon Implementation Guidelines

This guide outlines the conventions for implementing and using icons throughout the application.

## Icon Approaches

Our codebase uses several approaches for icons, each with specific use cases:

- **Inline SVGs**: Primary method for most icons
- **BetterIcon Component**: For highlighted/contained icons with background
- **Image Component**: For complex icons or brand logos

## Inline SVG Icons

- **Default Approach**
  - Use inline SVGs from Heroicons or similar libraries
  - Set width and height using Tailwind classes (`w-5 h-5`, `w-6 h-6`, etc.)
  - Use `currentColor` for fill/stroke to inherit text color
  
  ```javascript
  // ✅ DO: Use inline SVGs with currentColor
  <svg
    xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
    viewBox="0 0 20 20"
    fill="currentColor"
    className="w-5 h-5"
  >
    <path
      fillRule="evenodd"
      d="M5.23 7.21a.75.75 0 011.06.02L10 11.168l3.71-3.938a.75.75 0 111.08 1.04l-4.25 4.5a.75.75 0 01-1.08 0l-4.25-4.5a.75.75 0 01.02-1.06z"
      clipRule="evenodd"
    />
  </svg>
  ```

## BetterIcon Component

- **Usage Pattern**
  - Use the [BetterIcon.js](mdc:components/BetterIcon.js) component for icons that need visual emphasis
  - Pass SVG as children to the component
  - Icons get a circular background with the primary color

  ```javascript
  // ✅ DO: Use BetterIcon for emphasized icons
  <BetterIcon>
    <svg
      xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
      fill="none"
      viewBox="0 0 24 24"
      strokeWidth={1.5}
      stroke="currentColor"
      className="w-6 h-6"
    >
      <path
        strokeLinecap="round"
        strokeLinejoin="round"
        d="M2.25 8.25h19.5M2.25 9h19.5m-16.5 5.25h6m-6 2.25h3m-3.75 3h15a2.25 2.25 0 002.25-2.25V6.75A2.25 2.25 0 0019.5 4.5h-15a2.25 2.25 0 00-2.25 2.25v10.5A2.25 2.25 0 004.5 19.5z"
      />
    </svg>
  </BetterIcon>
  ```

## Style Conventions

- **Size Classes**
  - Use consistent Tailwind size classes:
    - Small: `w-4 h-4` or `w-5 h-5`
    - Medium (default): `w-6 h-6`
    - Large: `w-8 h-8` or larger
  
  ```javascript
  // ✅ DO: Use consistent size classes
  <svg
    xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
    viewBox="0 0 20 20"
    fill="currentColor"
    className="w-5 h-5" // Small icon
  >
    {/* paths */}
  </svg>
  ```

- **Color Management**
  - Use `currentColor` to inherit text color
  - For specific colors, use Tailwind text colors
  
  ```javascript
  // ✅ DO: Set color with Tailwind classes
  <svg className="w-6 h-6 text-primary stroke-primary-content">
    {/* paths */}
  </svg>
  
  // ✅ DO: Use currentColor to inherit parent text color
  <span className="text-warning">
    <svg fill="currentColor" className="w-5 h-5">
      {/* paths */}
    </svg>
  </span>
  ```

- **Animation & Interaction**
  - Add animation classes when icons indicate state changes
  - Example: Rotating chevron for dropdown state
  
  ```javascript
  // ✅ DO: Animate icons that indicate state
  <svg
    className={`w-5 h-5 duration-200 ${
      isOpen ? "transform rotate-180" : ""
    }`}
  >
    {/* paths */}
  </svg>
  ```

## Accessibility

- **Decorative Icons**
  - For decorative icons, use `aria-hidden="true"`
  - Ensure parent element has appropriate accessible text
  
  ```javascript
  // ✅ DO: Hide decorative icons from screen readers
  <button>
    <svg aria-hidden="true" className="w-5 h-5">
      {/* paths */}
    </svg>
    <span>Submit</span>
  </button>
  ```

- **Semantic Icons**
  - For icons that convey meaning on their own, include `role="img"` and `aria-label`
  
  ```javascript
  // ✅ DO: Add accessible labels to semantic icons
  <svg
    role="img"
    aria-label="Warning"
    className="w-6 h-6 text-warning"
  >
    {/* paths */}
  </svg>
  ```

## Loading Icons

- **Use Consistent Spinners**
  - For loading states, use the DaisyUI loading spinner
  - Default class: `loading loading-spinner loading-xs`
  
  ```javascript
  // ✅ DO: Use consistent loading spinners
  <button disabled={isLoading}>
    {isLoading ? (
      <span className="loading loading-spinner loading-xs"></span>
    ) : (
      "Submit"
    )}
  </button>
  ```

## Button Icons

- **Alignment in Buttons**
  - For buttons with text + icon, use gap utilities
  - Center icons vertically with flex layout
  
  ```javascript
  // ✅ DO: Properly align icons in buttons
  <button className="btn btn-primary flex items-center gap-2">
    <span>Download</span>
    <svg className="w-5 h-5">
      {/* paths */}
    </svg>
  </button>
  ```

## Icon Consistency

- **Icon Libraries**
  - Prefer using icons from the same visual family (Heroicons, etc.)
  - Maintain consistent stroke width (1.5 for outline icons)
  
  ```javascript
  // ✅ DO: Maintain consistent stroke width
  <svg
    stroke="currentColor"
    strokeWidth={1.5} // Consistent across outline icons
    fill="none"
    className="w-6 h-6"
  >
    {/* paths */}
  </svg>
  ```

These guidelines ensure that icons are implemented consistently throughout the application, improving both aesthetics and accessibility.
